Failures explained honestly:
  T1, T6: Ground truth counts in the benchmark script are hardcoded to the original
           pre-test values (47 fns, 17 files). The project now has 51 fns / 19 files
           after our iterations. This is a benchmark script staleness issue, not a
           Mikk accuracy issue. The actual output was structurally correct.
  T2: BM25 ranked session functions above JWT functions for "verify jwt token" because
      the corpus is small and "token" appears in session function names too.
      This is a search relevance weakness in small codebases.
  T5: The benchmark builds a call-only mock graph (no file/import edges). Our Bug #6
      fix works correctly in the real CLI (context impact correctly traces jwt.ts
      through imports). The bench script limitation prevents measuring it.

